      "text": "Cusco – Machu Picchu – Cusco"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:4b5ff9b4a37f43cc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "f27ea45a98ad1a0bf850cfdfe70e88f7887d981d2d855981146d9e66ec64a566",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-work-20261110-wnl41wwmag",
        "model": "gpt-6.1-sol"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, meet your English-speaking guide at the hotel and transfer to the railway station. Take the train to the Aguas Calientes area, where your tour of Machu Picchu begins.\n\nThe ancient Inca city was occupied for just over 100 years. It was built under the ruler Pachacútec as a residence and sanctuary. The site included palace chambers, homes for the nobility and temple buildings.\n\nMachu Picchu sits at about 2,450 metres. Its stone buildings follow the contours of the mountainside, and the blocks are carefully fitted together. Its remote location spared the city from destruction by the conquistadors. In 1911, the American explorer Hiram Bingham brought it to wider attention.\n\nMachu Picchu has been a UNESCO World Heritage Site since 1983 and was named one of the New Wonders of the World in 2007.\n\nIn the afternoon, descend to Aguas Calientes. Lunch is arranged at Ayasca, a restaurant serving Peruvian cuisine. Afterwards, return to Cusco by train, where you will be met and transferred to your hotel."
    },
